 evidence assessment**\n\nI want to keep my assessment comprehensive but concise, targeting an oververbosity of 6. I should organize my evidence findings into clear bullet points:\n\n- **Proven**: The seed configuration contains target parameters, but V480 logs are disabled, and checkpoints show target_parameters as null with differing config SHA.\n- **Proven**: V480 has shown weakness under the gate with bit regression and truncation in cp2/6.\n- **Plausible**: Omitted target_parameters potentially altered adapter architecture, affecting trainable coverage, causing regression.\n- **Unknown**: It\u2019s unclear whether the omitted tensors were not loaded, ignored, or retained, pending further review of the safetensors logs.\n- **Proven**: Eval_loss is insufficient; comparing V480\u2019s baseline of 0.9725 to the final 0.9739 reveals similar losses.\n- **Plausible**: Having the same file size with a different config poses risks since the loader relies on that config.\n- **Unknown**: Need clarity on the submission harness generation. I\u2019ll start listing potential root causes.**Exploring root causes for issues**\n\nI\u2019m analyzing several potential causes for the observed issues, along with confidence percentages. Firstly, I suspect the PEFT architecture discontinuity due to missing target_parameters could account for 35-45%. Next, there\u2019s an objective/metric mismatch, as loss tokens and exact answer accuracy don't align, which I estimate at 20-25%. Negative transfer related to data mixture imbalance might be around 15-20%. I also see 10-15% for mismatches in generation, template, and truncation. Lastly, bugs in adapter loading and logging could explain 5-10%, and I might need to include the accuracy=0 logging bug there.",
